From fharrell at virginia.edu  Wed May  6 01:04:25 1998
From: fharrell at virginia.edu (Frank E Harrell Jr)
Date: Tue, 05 May 1998 21:04:25 -0400
Subject: Re: [S] REPEATED MEASURES DESIGN
In-Reply-To: <3.0.32.19980506102407.006b16e8@clyde.its.unimelb.edu.au>
Message-ID: <01bd788a$e9c28020$3d1a85ce@feh3kpc>

In the Hmisc library in Statlib you'll find the rm.boot function which
is for repeated measures data.  It uses the bootstrap to get pointwise,
or even better, simultaneous confidence bands around time profiles.
By using simultaneous confidence bands you have an adjustment
for multiple looks at the data (multiple time points).  If each subject
receives 2 treatments, you will have to take the point-by-point
differences between treatments as the raw data to use rm.boot.
rm.boot uses regression splines to model time trends.  See the
document by Alzola  & Harrell on our web page (under Stat Computing
Tools) for examples with graphical output.

Other facilities in S-Plus will let you do formal parametric modeling
for your problem.  

