> Windows.   I realize this may be a minor nit to pick, but oughtn't this be
> a startup option?

Here's how I set up persistent window placement within S-PLUS 4.0

  1. Start S-PLUS

  2. Arrange the windows the way you want them to always appear
     (for me, the "Commands" and "Object Browser" windows are tiled vertically)

  3. For each window:
       i.  Left-Click on the Title Bar
       ii. Select the menu command: Option|Save Window Size/Properties as 
Default

     Note that for the "Object Browser" window, after you Left-Click on the
     Title Bar, make sure none of the elements (e.g. "Data Frame") in the 
     "Object Browser" window are selected... because you will not have access to
     the "Option|Save Window Size/Properties as Default" menu command if any are
     selected. Instead, you will see something like
     "Option|Save Data Frame Properties as Default"

     To unselect any highlighted elements in the "Object Browser" window, 
     Left-Click on the white background in the "Object Browser" window.

