Full text search capability does not function properly with the S-PLUS 4.5
help files. The problem manifests itself as follows:

If you click the Find tab in the Help Topics dialog that appears when
you launch S-PLUS Help, you will see a Find Setup Wizard. If you attempt
to use the Wizard, you will eventually get the following message from
Windows: "There is not enough memory available for this task. Quit
one or more programs to increase available memory, and then try again. (2)"

We believe the error message is erroneous; increasing your memory will not
allow you to successfully construct the full text database. However, we are
still not sure exactly what the problem is, nor how easy it will be to fix.
