From zaslavsk at hcp.med.harvard.edu  Wed May 20 18:24:05 1998
From: zaslavsk at hcp.med.harvard.edu (Alan Zaslavsky)
Date: Wed, 20 May 1998 14:24:05 -0400
Subject: Re: [S] bug? values of vector elements changed by logical operation on the elements
In-Reply-To: <D1B7E20D0302D111A1C800609769E5DC0E07CF@nki.rfmh.org>
Message-ID: <199805201824.OAA08314@nightingale.med.harvard.edu>

Thank you, you have provided ammunition for my (totally fruitless and
by now lost) argument that the use of "<-" for assignment is an
atrocity.  You got bitten in these lines:

> out2[13] <- as.numeric(out2[5] <- 66.667 & out2[8] > -66.667)
> out2[14] <- as.numeric(out2[9] <- 66.667 & out2[12] > -66.667)

The <- is interpreted as assignment, so the expression 

                66.667 & out2[8] > -66.667

is evaluated (to T) and assigned into out2[5] (where it is coerced to
numeric as a 1), and similarly on the next line.

If you had written it as:

> out2[13] <- as.numeric(out2[5] < -66.667 & out2[8] > -66.667)
> out2[14] <- as.numeric(out2[9] < -66.667 & out2[12] > -66.667)

then I think you would have been OK.
