Subject: Re: [S] Assignment arrow.
In-Reply-To: <199805201836.PAA07307@tanner.math.unb.ca>
Message-ID: <9805220302.AA28932@joker>

As a point of historical interest, back in the mid-70's, some
terminals had a key with an arrow on it.  Early versions of S used
this key as the assignment operator.  Over time, fewer keyboards
had the arrow, replacing it with the underscore, and assigning it the
same ascii code.  So _ for assignment is really a backward
compatibility issue because it used to print as -> .

Today I use -> with spaces around it...  And I always put two spaces
after a period at the end of a sentence.

Alan Gross
